One abvioius use for the empty bottles is for the water which are easily
accessible from fountain, sink, pool, etc.  I also remember someone
suggested a "tap" in the dugeon.  Maybe for potion of booze?  

How about making juice out of those juicy corpses!!!

Yeah, I know it's sick, but hey, everyone has eaten those lizards, rats,
bats, zombies (!), and even human!!!  And also some of us have made tins
out of them using tinning kit (sounds so innocent, but imagine...)

Why we want to do that?  I guess I have to give it a better reason than
just the satisfaction.  Let's carry around those juicers (mixer? ok, how
about juicing kit :-) that extracts the intrinsics out of those monsters.
The difference between the tins will be that juice have no nutritional
value, much less weight, and the bottles can be reused after you quaff from
it.  You can also make existing potions out of some of the corpses.

For example:
	giant juice - potion of gain strength.
	wraith juice - potion of gain level
	bat juice - potion of confusion
	violet fungi juice - potion of hallucination
	kobold juice - potion of sickness
	etc.

Below aren't really true, since they are their attack types, not their
intrinsics, but...

	floating eye juice - potion of paralysis (you might need it)
	umber hulk juice - potion of confusion 

What the heck,
	nurse juice - potion of extra healing


OK, just a thought.


